{"hw":"ὅστε","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">ὅστε</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">ὅστε</span>, <span class=\"gk\">ἥτε, ὅτε</span> (also written divisim), in <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hom.</span> </span> also <span class=\"lex-orth gk\">ὅ τε</span> as masc., <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">17.757</span> </span>: (<span class=\"lex-etym gk\">ὅς, τε</span>):—<div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">who, which,</b> <abbr>like</abbr> the simple <span class=\"gk\">ὅς</span> or <span class=\"gk\">ὅστις,</span> freq. with a generalizing force (<span class=\"lex-itype gk\">τε</span> is however sts. otiose, as in <span class=\"gk\">ὅτε, ὥστε, οἷός τε, ἐπεί τε,</span> etc., <abbr>v.</abbr> <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">τε</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">B.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1</span> </span>), <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">14.221</span> </span>, etc.: neut. pl. <span class=\"gk\">τά τε</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">5.481</span> </span>, etc.: pl. fem. <span class=\"gk\">τάς τε</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">11.554</span> </span>: used also in <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">P.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.39</span> </span>, al., and lyr. passages of Trag. (<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pers.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">16</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ag.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">49</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ch.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">615</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">El.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">151</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Tr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">824</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">E.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Hec.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">445</span> </span>), but very rare in trim., <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pers.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">297</span> </span>,<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">762</span> </span>,<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Eu.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">25</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1024</span> </span>; and in Prose only in special forms, such as <span class=\"gk\">ἅτε, ἐφ' ᾧτε</span>:—rarely with antec. expressed, <span class=\"gk\">θεάων τάων, αἵ τ'</span>.. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">5.332</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τῷ ἴκελος, ὅν τ'</span>.. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">24.758</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τά τε φρονέων, ἅ τ' ἐγώπερ</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7.312</span> </span>.—Not to be confounded with <span class=\"gk\">ὅς τε,</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">and who,</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.365</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">3.185</span> </span>,al. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">2</span> <span class=\"gk\">ἐξ οὗτε</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">from the</b> <b class=\"lex-tr\">time when</b>.., <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pers.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">762</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Eu.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">25</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἀπ' οὗτε</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">PCair.Zen.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">291.3</span> </span> <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">(iii B. C.)</span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">3</span> freq. folld. by <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">περ</span> <span class=\"gk\">, τά τε στυγέουσι θεοίπερ</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">20.65</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">4</span> with <span class=\"gk\">ῥα</span> between <span class=\"gk\">ὅς</span> and <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">τε</span> <span class=\"gk\">, αἴγειρος ὥς, ἥ ῥά τε</span>.. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.483</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">15.411</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">19.31</span> </span>, al. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> <span class=\"gk\">ὅ τε</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">in that, because</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.244</span> </span>; introducing the reason for making a statement or asking a question, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.32</span> </span>, al.; so prob. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">15.468</span> </span>: for <span class=\"gk\">ἅτε, ᾧτε</span>, <abbr>v.</abbr> sub vocc.: <span class=\"gk\">ᾇτε</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Dor.</span> </span> for <span class=\"gk\">ᾗτε</span>, <b class=\"lex-tr\">as</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Lys.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1308</span> </span> (lyr.): <span class=\"gk\">ἐφ' ᾧτε</span>, v. ἐπί <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">B.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">111.3</span> </span>.</div></div>"}